{"abstract":[{"text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"],"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"import GrafluentCollections","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and can be imported on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import GrafluentCollections","","var scores: FenwickTree = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]","print(scores.prefixSum(through: 3))  \/\/ 9","print(scores.sum(in: 2 ..< 6))       \/\/ 19"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Values-not-references","text":"Values, not references"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every collection is a copy-on-write struct. Assigning one copies nothing until one of the copies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is mutated; then only that copy pays, once, and the other keeps its elements:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let original: BTree = [1, 2, 3]","var copy = original","copy.insert(4)","Array(original)   \/\/ [1, 2, 3]","Array(copy)       \/\/ [1, 2, 3, 4]"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices of a tree live in flat arrays linked by integer indices rather than in a class per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, so a copy is a few array copies and a traversal reads memory almost in order. The API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"follows the standard library and Swift Collections: the sorted sets are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SetAlgebra"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"random-access collections indexed by rank, the dictionaries take "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subscript(_:default:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range trees are collections of their values."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Traps-and-checked-spellings","text":"Traps and checked spellings"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A plain spelling traps when its precondition fails, like an "},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" subscript out of range: it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fast path, for callers who know the precondition holds. Beside it, a "},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" spelling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws a typed error instead, one of those in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" turns it into an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let primes: AVLTree = [2, 3, 5, 7]","primes[2]                    \/\/ 5","try primes[checked: 9]       \/\/ throws IndexOutOfRange"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A mutation that would break a structure’s invariant, such as joining two treaps whose elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interleave, throws on its plain spelling and changes nothing. Where the standard library’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collections return an optional (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(_:)"},{"text":", a dictionary’s subscript, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"min()"},{"text":"), these do too.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Grafluent-conversions","text":"Grafluent conversions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A collection whose shape is a tree converts to the Grafluent type of that shape: ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"PrefixTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with an initializer on the Grafluent type that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"costs O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":") once. Structures whose shape is a general graph, such as decision diagrams and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automata, offer a view that is a Grafluent graph without copying. Either way, Grafluent’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms, drawings and file formats run over the collection; its own operations never go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the conversion. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"},{"text":" shows the round trip.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Modules","text":"Modules"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Group"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Modules"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Search trees","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (AVL, red–black and splay trees, treaps), "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (B-trees), "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (skip lists)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tries","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/tries","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (tries over any sequence of symbols, radix and Patricia trees, Aho–Corasick automata)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Suffix structures","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/suffixstructures"},{"type":"text","text":" (suffix arrays with LCP, suffix trees, suffix automata)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Decision diagrams","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams"},{"type":"text","text":" (reduced ordered BDDs, zero-suppressed ZDDs)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Range and spatial trees","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/rangetrees","type":"reference"},{"text":" (Fenwick trees, segment trees with lazy propagation, interval trees), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/spatialtrees","type":"reference"},{"text":" (k-d trees, quadtrees, octrees)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sequences and persistence"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/ropes","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (ropes: sequences as balanced trees of chunks), "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (path-copying weight-balanced trees that keep every version)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Caches"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/caches"},{"type":"text","text":" (LRU caches)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shared"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"CollectionErrors","type":"codeVoice"}],"overridingTitle":"CollectionErrors","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors","type":"reference"},{"text":": the errors the ","type":"text"},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" spellings throw, re-exported by every module that throws them","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"